title: Toor Dal
method: stovetop
source: https://www.tarladalal.com/basic-toovar-dal-recipe-toor-dal-42289r
protein: legumes
ingredient_count: 13
---

  Combine the @toovar (arhar) dal{3/4%cup}(washed and drained), @onion{1/4%cup}(chopped), @tomato{1/4%cup}(chopped), @green chilli{1}(slit), @turmeric powder (haldi){1/2%tsp} and @water{2%cups} in a #pressure cooker{}. Mix well and pressure cook for 3 whistles.

Allow the steam to escape before opening the lid.

Remove the slit green chilli, add @water{1%cup} and @salt{to taste} and whisk well. Keep aside.

Heat the @oil{1%tbsp} in a deep #non-stick pan{}.

Add the @cumin seeds (jeera){1/2%tsp}, @garlic (lehsun){4}(crushed), @asafoetida (hing){1/4%tsp} and @curry leaves (kadi patta){4} and sauté on a medium flame for ~{30%seconds}.

Add the @whole dry Kashmiri red chilli{2}(broken into pieces) and sauté on a medium flame for ~{30%seconds}.

Add the dal mixture, mix well and cook on a medium flame for ~{3-4%minutes}, while stirring occasionally.

Add the @coriander (dhania){2%tbsp}(chopped) and mix well.

Serve the toovar dal hot.